<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="match-rules" data-rev="0">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/rules/default.json, tuning.json, README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Rule pack version 2 with an added_time block (seconds per stoppage kind, card seconds, variance, minimum, cap of 900 seconds) and min_players 7; the foul, card, and dead-ball tuning fields; the modder reference rewritten because the engine now enforces the pack.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>content/</td><td>+80 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/data/attributes.rs, data/rules.rs, player.rs, tuning.rs, error.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">aggression becomes a required attribute; AddedTime and min_players with garde ranges; Player gains status and yellow count; EngineError::Snapshot names the refusal reason.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+130 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/rules/mod.rs, clock.rs, offside.rs, fouls.rs, restart.rs, discipline.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The referee: live play, dead ball, and full time; the stoppage hook; the match clock and the added-time formula with seeded variance; the offside set computed at a pass and judged at the first touch; the three-way tackle roll and the card roll; restart spots, targets, and takers; bookings, sending-off, reshape to ten, abandonment below seven.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src/rules</td><td>+900</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, decision.rs, team.rs, pitch.rs, rng.rs, validate.rs, record.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The wall bounce is replaced by exit detection and restarts; run plays to full time or the announced maximum; TickSink::on_stoppage; decisions suspended during a dead ball; team reshape and side switch; law geometry; generator state through the word position; validator exemptions and the restart-spot rule; tick-file schema 4.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+471 / -63</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/snapshot.rs, scenario.rs; Cargo.toml, lib.rs (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">The binary snapshot: header, body with every Simulation field except scratch and drained events, trailer with body length and SHA-256; atomic replace by rename; a fail-closed reader that names bad magic, unknown version, truncation, checksum, build, and content mismatches. The scenario builder exists only under a test feature.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+466</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine/src/observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">match-stats gains stats.fouls, stats.offsides, stats.corners, rules.pack_version, cards, added time, ticks played, snapshot writes, dead-ball ticks, offside checks; run-report gains ticks per match and processor time per tick.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src/observe</td><td>+45</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/rules_offside.rs, rules_fouls.rs, rules_cards.rs, rules_restarts.rs, rules_clock.rs, snapshot.rs; common/mod.rs, content.rs, full_match.rs, validator.rs (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">One criterion file per law group, each built on a scripted scene; the continuation test compares tick records byte for byte from the snapshot tick; full_match holds a sanity band for fouls, corners, throw-ins, and offsides.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/tests</td><td>+840 / -8</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol/src/event.rs, lib.rs, command.rs, message.rs; docs/reference/protocol.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Nine event types and six optional fields (player.id, player.secondary_id, card.kind, foul.advantage, minute.added, added_time.s); PROTOCOL_VERSION 2 because ticks_expected now means the maximum; comments rewritten without slice names; the reference document updated so its test passes.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/protocol and docs</td><td>+84 / -15</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/cli.rs, main.rs, resume.rs (new), simulate.rs, serve.rs, stream_run.rs, record.rs, bench.rs; tests/resume.rs (new)</summary><div class="pl-card">engine-cli resume --snapshot; snapshots at every stoppage from simulate and serve; the maximum announced everywhere; the new events mapped to the wire; bench reports ticks per match and processor time per tick with no snapshot on the timed path.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+352 / -19</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/stoppages.mjs, main.mjs, tests/stoppages.test.mjs; README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The stoppage index takes restart frames plus only the events that stop play; the scrubber maximum becomes the last tick at full time; the README names the laws, the snapshot location, and resume.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web/ and root</td><td>+68 / -4</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Processor time per tick exceeds the 10 percent tripwire</div><div class="callout-body">Offside is computed only at a pass and exit detection is two comparisons. Step 22 measures three drives before the tests are finalised; the limit is 1.566 microseconds per tick and 6.69 MB. A miss goes to the product owner; no law is removed silently.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · A resumed match drifts from the uninterrupted one</div><div class="callout-body">Exact continuation fails if one field is missing from the snapshot. The continuation test compares tick records byte for byte from the snapshot tick, and a write-read-write test catches a field that does not round-trip.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · Restart positioning fights the steering agents</div><div class="callout-body">Decisions are suspended during a dead ball, encroaching opponents target the 9.15 m circle, and a restart is taken at three times the delay at the latest; rules.dead_ball_ticks shows a stall.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · Earlier tick files and the local fixture are refused</div><div class="callout-body">PROTOCOL_VERSION 2 and tick schema 4 refuse earlier files. None is in the repository; step 23 regenerates the local fixture, and each refusal names both versions.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · A sent-off marker sits beside the pitch</div><div class="callout-body">The tick record holds 22 positions and no status bit, so a sent-off player parks at a fixed spot outside the play surface until viewer-match-day hides parked markers.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R6 · Foul, card, and added-time rates are estimates</div><div class="callout-body">full_match.rs holds a sanity band only; the calibration slice tunes the rates against real league figures.</div></aside>
  </div>
